        <obo:IAO_0000115>The photochemically induced addition of a hydrosilane across the double bond of an alkene or alkyne to give a more substituted silane, usually applied to cases where the hydrosilane is part of a silicon surface. The reaction uses UV irradiation and is usually initiated by an added photoactive compound such as a platinum catalyst.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>photo-hydrosilylation</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>RXNO</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
