        <obo:IAO_0000115>A chemical reaction in which a carboxylic acid (or its salt) reacts with an organic (alkyl or aryl) halide to form a new carbon-carbon bond with concomitant loss of CO2. In addition, the reaction requires a metal catalyst, a base and an oxidizing agent.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <dcterms:creator rdf:resource="http://orcid.org/0000-0002-4378-6061"/>
        <dcterms:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-12-06T08:44:51Z</dcterms:date>
